// Priya Nair: a primary-school teacher at the school up the hill. Friendship only. Arrives in chapter 1.
// Cheerful, organised, perpetually covered in glitter. Knot names follow Docs/ADDING_CONTENT.md, "Dialogue".

=== priya_visit ===
Priya: Hello! I'm Priya, I teach the little ones up at St. Brigid's. # happy
~ note(Teaches the youngest class at St. Brigid's: twenty-eight children.)
Priya: I've heard this shop has a pattern for everything. I have a class of twenty-eight. I need everything.
-> END

=== priya_visit_glitter ===
Priya: Sorry, I'm shedding glitter. It's not a choice anymore, it's a lifestyle. # happy
-> END

=== priya_visit_marking ===
Priya: Forty-two spelling tests to mark. Someone spelled "because" with a Z. # thoughtful
Priya: Twice. In different places. I'm almost impressed.
-> END

=== priya_visit_1_assembly ===
Priya: We're doing an assembly about the sea. I'm a jellyfish. # neutral
Priya: I didn't volunteer. Nobody volunteers to be a jellyfish.
-> END

=== priya_visit_2_kids ===
Priya: One of my class asked if you were a witch. I said no. # happy
Priya: Then she asked if you could teach her to be one, so I've told her about cross stitch instead.
-> END

=== priya_visit_3_tea ===
Priya: Half term! I have a whole week to finish sentences. # happy
Priya: I'm going to start with this one: thank you for always being open when I'm passing.
-> END

=== priya_request_classroom ===
# fits: sampler, hoop_art, tablecloth
# best: sampler
Priya: Our reading corner is a beanbag and a sad rug. # thoughtful
Priya: I want the children to walk in and feel like it's a special place. Something cheerful on the wall?
-> END

=== priya_request_fair ===
# fits: tablecloth, tote, plushie_sewn
# best: tablecloth
Priya: The school fair's coming. Our stall has a trestle table that looks like it's survived a war. # neutral
Priya: Something to make it look loved, so people actually stop.
-> END

=== priya_request_mascot ===
# fits: plushie, plushie_sewn, hoop_art
# best: plushie
Priya: The class wants a mascot. They voted for "a crab called Kevin". # happy
Priya: Democracy is beautiful and terrifying.
-> END

=== priya_handover_good ===
Priya: Oh, they are going to LOSE their minds. In a good way. Mostly in a good way. # happy
-> END

=== priya_handover_good_star ===
Priya: Gold star. No, really, I carry them. Here. # happy
She sticks a gold star on your sleeve.
-> END

=== priya_handover_okay ===
Priya: Lovely! It'll be covered in fingerprints by Tuesday, so this is perfect. # happy
-> END

=== priya_handover_poor ===
Priya: The children won't mind. Children love things that look homemade. It's adults who are the problem. # thoughtful
-> END

=== priya_scene_1 ===
Priya: Can I tell you something silly? # thoughtful
Priya: I wanted to run a shop like this when I was little. I had a cardboard till and everything.
~ note(Dreamed of running a shop like this as a child.)
* [What happened?]
    Priya: Teacher training happened. And I love it, I do. But sometimes I walk past here and wonder. # sad
    ~ friendship(5)
* [You could still learn to stitch.]
    Priya: You think? Even me? I can't even cut in a straight line. # surprised
    ~ friendship(5)
- Priya: Anyway. Thanks for listening. Teachers mostly get talked at.
-> END

=== priya_scene_2 ===
Priya: The class made you something. # happy
She hands you a card. Twenty-eight wobbly names, and a drawing of the shop with you in the window, enormous.
Priya: They insisted you be the biggest. I didn't argue.
* [Tell them it's going on the wall.]
    Priya: They'll be unbearable. Thank you. # happy
    ~ friendship(10)
* [Is that a crab?]
    Priya: That's Kevin. Kevin goes everywhere now. # happy
    ~ friendship(5)
-> END

=== priya_scene_3 ===
Priya: I've signed up for evening classes. # surprised
Priya: Stitching. At Knot & Needle. Don't be cross! Rowan was very persuasive.
~ note(Takes evening stitching classes at Knot & Needle.)
* [I'm proud of you.]
    Priya: Really? Oh good. I was worried you'd think I'd defected. # happy
    ~ friendship(10)
* [Come here on Thursdays instead. I'll teach you.]
    Priya: You'd do that? I'll bring biscuits. Every week. That's a promise. # happy
    ~ friendship(15)
-> END
